<article class="env-lemma" id="0473">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0473">Lemma <span data-tag="0473">29.32.4</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z \ar[r]_ i \ar[d]_ f &  X \ar[d]^ g \\  Z' \ar[r]^{i'} &  X' }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a fibre product diagram in the category of schemes with $i$, $i'$ immersions. Then the canonical map $f^*\mathcal{C}_{Z'/X'} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/01R4" data-tag="01R4">29.32.3</a> is surjective. If $g$ is flat, then it is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $R' \to R$ be a ring map, and $I' \subset R'$ an ideal. Set $I = I'R$. Then $I'/(I')^2 \otimes _{R'} R \to I/I^2$ is surjective. If $R' \to R$ is flat, then $I = I' \otimes _{R'} R$ and $I^2 = (I')^2 \otimes _{R'} R$ and we see the map is an isomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>